---
import "@skryensya/core/components/tag.css";
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ComponentPreview from "../../../components/ComponentPreview.astro";
import { tagTree } from "../../../demos/tag";
import { getLocale, useTranslations } from "../../../i18n";

const t = useTranslations(getLocale(Astro.url));

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/react`;


---

<Base title="Tag" description="Tag: optionally removable keyword chip, with tones and React component.">
  <h1>Tag</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Tag classifies content that the user can act on: filters, facets, chips. Where <a href="/en/components/badge">Badge</a> is a read-only status tag, Tag is more square (control radius, not pill) to be read as actionable, and may carry a remove button.
  </p>

  <ComponentPreview tree={tagTree(t)} label="Tag" />
  <p>
    When removable, the tag and the remove button are two different targets: the control's accessible name names the tag it removes.
  </p>

  <h2>The X is a Button, not a drawing of one</h2>
  <p>
    The remove control is an actual <a href="/en/components/button">Button</a> — <code>sk-button sk-interactive</code> with <code>data-size="sm"</code>, <code>data-icon-only</code>, and <code>data-variant="ghost"</code> — and <code>sk-tag__remove</code> is just the modifier that shrinks it to the height of the capsule. Tag does not send its own interaction.
  </p>
  <p>
    What you gain is what you no longer have to maintain here: the hover and the press come from the <a href="/en/state-layer">state layer</a>, the focus ring is the same as all the controls, and the touch area reaches <strong>44px</strong> by the <code>:: after</code> of the button even though the face paints 20px. Before they were 20px for face and 20px for useful white.
  </p>
  <p>
    The color is still <code>currentColor</code>, so each shade brings its X in its own color without a per-tone rule.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview. <code>onRemove</code> is optional.</p>
</Base>
